  "narrative": "I am María Fernanda Pérez Rodríguez, a Venezuelan citizen born on May 14, 1990, in Caracas. I am applying for asylum because I was persecuted in my country for my political opinion. In 2019, I actively participated in protests against the government. In April 2019, during a march in Caracas, I was beaten by members of armed pro-government colectivos. I subsequently received death threats at my home and at my workplace. I feared for my life and decided to leave the country in December 2022. I entered the United States on January 12, 2023, through El Paso, Texas. If I return to Venezuela, I fear being detained, tortured, or killed because of my history of opposition political activity. I respectfully request that asylum be granted to me.",
